  "worked_solution": "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=6.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(6)=-2+9=7\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=7.$",
